nese heroes are about to get some  backup from international heroes  meaning that deku will finally be able  to take a break  endeavor reminds deku that he is the key  to everything  he is the one that all for one wants to  get his hands on  so it is absolutely unacceptable to have  deku  die on them they need deku but we all  know what  deku is like we know him as a person and  we know that he will never just  take a break when he knows that innocent  civilians are suffering  and that brings us to a very serious  problem  with deku's personality a problem that  could bring about his tragic  end we know that deku doesn't want to  kill anyone not even villains  and he wants to save everyone that's his  whole thing  however the manga has already pointed  out on numerous occasions  that in his rush to save others deku  often neglects his own  health and safety he will go to any  lengths to be heroic he will push his  body beyond its limits  over and over again and eventually that  heroism  could be the very thing that kills him  this idea  is very much stressed yet again in the  latest chapter  and it's something that we have to pay  close attention to  in the end deku's worst enemy may not be  any villain  at all he may end up being his own worst  enemy  yes what deku is doing is noble and  heroic  but if he ends up destroying himself and  his own body in the process  of trying to be a hero and save everyone  he won't be able to save anyone anymore  although by acting this way deku is  definitely going to earn  the respect of stain and you just know  that stain is still out there lurking  and watching all of these events unfold  as you probably guessed deck who tells  endeavor that he cannot give the  villains time to prepare so he won't  take breaks and he will continue to  fight even the vestiges of the former  one for all users  are urging deku to chill out and take  some time to allow his wounds to heal  but deku seems to ignore them as well  danger sense tells him that there is a  threat nearby  and he rushes off to meet it the  situation is getting so bad  that the vestiges decide to call a  meeting amongst themselves  in order to discuss deku's situation  everyone is seated down in a chair  except for the second user who is still  standing off to the side  presumably the second user still hasn't  fully come around to everyone else's  plan  but he is certainly more willing to  engage than he was before  and while all of the other vestiges are  worried about deku pushing himself  too hard the second user believes that  deku is actually  on the right path in this time of  extreme crisis  deku has a duty to keep pushing himself  in order to save the  innocent nevertheless the second user  believes that there is something that  the vestiges  can do to help protect deku  but we don't get to find out what that  thing is  because the focus of the chapter then  shifts to deku fighting a bunch of  villains  in the real world the regular people on  the streets are actually freaked out by  deku when they first  see him both because of his new darker  appearance and because of the fact that  he is clearly using  multiple quirks the people are worried  that deku might be one of all for one's  subordinates  but he assures them that he is not and  of course his actions clearly  demonstrate that he is no  villain he is going out of his way to  protect civilians from the villains  but he just isn't doing it through the  official pro hero system  throughout it all deku is being driven  by the strong desire to find all for one  and the league of villains and to stop  them from causing more harm to the  people of japan  by the way the deku keeps talking about  needing to find them  and needing to stop them it seems as if  this might be turning into a bit of an  obsession  deku continues to take on more and more  strong villains  all the while thinking about all the  people in his life that he needs to  protect  all of the people that he wants